    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The prioritization of political messaging over mere aesthetic beauty is a fundamental shift toward art as a tool for social critique, which is a distinctly modern and post-modern development. Art's value has moved from being a contemplation of form to being an active intervention in the socio-political landscape. This means that the effectiveness of the message, its ability to challenge power structures, is now a primary metric of its success, not just its visual appeal.",
      "source": "target",
